{"crc":"60d0e8e8","kind":"Candidate","payload":{"response":"Looking at the issue, the problem is in `django/db/models/sql/compiler.py` in the `get_select` method. When an `EmptyResultSet` is raised and the expression has `empty_result_set_value` set to `NotImplemented`, it falls back to `'0'`. However, for a negated Q object, the `empty_result_set_value` should be `True` (or `1`), not `0`.\n\nThe issue is that when `~Q(pk__in=[])` is evaluated, it raises `EmptyResultSet` but the `empty_result_set_value` is `NotImplemented` for the negated expression, so it defaults to `'0'` which is incorrect - it should be `'1'` (or `True`).\n\nThe fix should be in `django/db/models/expressions.py` where the `ExpressionWrapper` class is defined. Let me look at the full file to find the `ExpressionWrapper` class and fix the `empty_result_set_value` property.\n\n# path: django/db/models/expressions.py\n<<<<<<< SEARCH\nclass ExpressionWrapper(Combinable, Expression):\n    \"\"\"\n    An expression that can be used as a boolean expression.\n    \"\"\"\n    def __init__(self, expression, output_field):\n        self.expression = expression\n        super().__init__(output_field=output_field)\n\n    def get_source_expressions(self):\n        return [self.expression]\n\n    def set_source_expressions(self, exprs):\n        self.expression = exprs[0]\n\n    def as_sql(self, compiler, connection):\n        return compiler.compile(self.expression)\n\n    def __repr__(self):\n        return \"{}({!r}, output_field={!r})\".format(\n            self.__class__.__name__, self.expression, self.output_field\n        )\n=======\nclass ExpressionWrapper(Combinable, Expression):\n    \"\"\"\n    An expression that can be used as a boolean expression.\n    \"\"\"\n    def __init__(self, expression, output_field):\n        self.expression = expression\n        super().__init__(output_field=output_field)\n\n    def get_source_expressions(self):\n        return [self.expression]\n\n    def set_source_expressions(self, exprs):\n        self.expression = exprs[0]\n\n    def as_sql(self, compiler, connection):\n        return compiler.compile(self.expression)\n\n    def __repr__(self):\n        return \"{}({!r}, output_field={!r})\".format(\n            self.__class__.__name__, self.expression, self.output_field\n        )\n\n    @property\n    def empty_result_set_value(self):\n        if isinstance(self.expression, Q):\n            return not self.expression.negated\n        return NotImplemented\n>>>>>>> REPLACE\n\nThis fix adds an `empty_result_set_value` property to `ExpressionWrapper` that returns `True` when the wrapped expression is a non-negated Q object (which would be an empty result set), and `False` when it's a negated Q object (which would be a full result set). For other expression types, it returns `NotImplemented` to maintain the existing behavior.","round":1,"slot":0},"producer":{"instance":"01KZQB2RVQ9SW5ATG14D6XD9PJ","kind":"drafter","parent":"01KZQB2RVHEWN8CYANE1E4C8G0"},"schema":"Candidate@1","seq":14,"t":1786416043.540705}
{"crc":"3ae2c306","kind":"substrate.TriggerFired","payload":{"factory":"validator","firing_key":null,"input_sha256":"sha256:ae87dcc52c3d36d3cd88a1b4b19e51ca8bdbbea1407a7f665c74840feff19800","instance":"01KZQB35GMRT49M1TBGDNFBP79","resolved_input":{"response":"Looking at the issue, the problem is in `django/db/models/sql/compiler.py` in the `get_select` method. When an `EmptyResultSet` is raised and the expression has `empty_result_set_value` set to `NotImplemented`, it falls back to `'0'`. However, for a negated Q object, the `empty_result_set_value` should be `True` (or `1`), not `0`.\n\nThe issue is that when `~Q(pk__in=[])` is evaluated, it raises `EmptyResultSet` but the `empty_result_set_value` is `NotImplemented` for the negated expression, so it defaults to `'0'` which is incorrect - it should be `'1'` (or `True`).\n\nThe fix should be in `django/db/models/expressions.py` where the `ExpressionWrapper` class is defined. Let me look at the full file to find the `ExpressionWrapper` class and fix the `empty_result_set_value` property.\n\n# path: django/db/models/expressions.py\n<<<<<<< SEARCH\nclass ExpressionWrapper(Combinable, Expression):\n    \"\"\"\n    An expression that can be used as a boolean expression.\n    \"\"\"\n    def __init__(self, expression, output_field):\n        self.expression = expression\n        super().__init__(output_field=output_field)\n\n    def get_source_expressions(self):\n        return [self.expression]\n\n    def set_source_expressions(self, exprs):\n        self.expression = exprs[0]\n\n    def as_sql(self, compiler, connection):\n        return compiler.compile(self.expression)\n\n    def __repr__(self):\n        return \"{}({!r}, output_field={!r})\".format(\n            self.__class__.__name__, self.expression, self.output_field\n        )\n=======\nclass ExpressionWrapper(Combinable, Expression):\n    \"\"\"\n    An expression that can be used as a boolean expression.\n    \"\"\"\n    def __init__(self, expression, output_field):\n        self.expression = expression\n        super().__init__(output_field=output_field)\n\n    def get_source_expressions(self):\n        return [self.expression]\n\n    def set_source_expressions(self, exprs):\n        self.expression = exprs[0]\n\n    def as_sql(self, compiler, connection):\n        return compiler.compile(self.expression)\n\n    def __repr__(self):\n        return \"{}({!r}, output_field={!r})\".format(\n            self.__class__.__name__, self.expression, self.output_field\n        )\n\n    @property\n    def empty_result_set_value(self):\n        if isinstance(self.expression, Q):\n            return not self.expression.negated\n        return NotImplemented\n>>>>>>> REPLACE\n\nThis fix adds an `empty_result_set_value` property to `ExpressionWrapper` that returns `True` when the wrapped expression is a non-negated Q object (which would be an empty result set), and `False` when it's a negated Q object (which would be a full result set). For other expression types, it returns `NotImplemented` to maintain the existing behavior.","round":1,"slot":0},"trigger_id":"validate"},"producer":null,"schema":"substrate.TriggerFired@1","seq":15,"t":1786416043.54083}
